            <title>Version 1.8.0</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 12:34:59 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>30</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.8.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[
                <h3>What's New in v1.8.0</h3>
<h4>Changed</h4>
<ul>
    <li>Major CPU usage reduction for long-running sessions. MacVitals no longer periodically spikes CPU usage while sitting in the background — previously it would briefly burn significant CPU roughly once a minute; that's now essentially eliminated.</li>
    <li>The process list is now updated far more efficiently under the hood, substantially cutting the CPU cost of routine refreshes — especially noticeable if you keep the window open for extended periods.</li>
    <li>Sitting idle for days no longer causes CPU or memory usage to slowly climb — MacVitals is now safe to leave running continuously for weeks at a time.</li>
</ul>
<h4>Fixed</h4>
<ul>
    <li>Fixed the memory delta time windows (30s / 1m / 2m / 5m) so each one now actually reflects the time span shown in its label.</li>
</ul>
            ]]></description>
